Threat Hunting Investigation
Objective
You are a Security Analyst tasked with investigating suspicious activity using system logs.
Your goal is to:
Identify malicious behaviour
Build a threat hunting hypothesis
Reconstruct the attack
Recommend response actions
Dataset
Analyse the following logs:
2026-04-30 08:55:12 LOGIN_SUCCESS user=john ip=102.89.34.12 location=Abuja
2026-04-30 09:02:45 LOGIN_FAILED user=john ip=185.203.116.45 location=Germany
2026-04-30 09:03:01 LOGIN_FAILED user=john ip=185.203.116.45 location=Germany
2026-04-30 09:04:10 LOGIN_SUCCESS user=john ip=185.203.116.45 location=Germany
2026-04-30 09:06:15 PROCESS_START user=john process=powershell.exe -nop -w hidden
2026-04-30 09:07:10 PROCESS_START user=john process=whoami.exe
2026-04-30 09:08:30 PROCESS_START user=john process=ipconfig
2026-04-30 09:09:10 OUTBOUND_CONNECTION src=192.168.1.10 dst=45.77.12.90 port=443
2026-04-30 09:10:05 DATA_TRANSFER src=192.168.1.10 dst=45.77.12.90 size=12MB

Tasks
Task 1 – Identify Suspicious Activity
List at least 5 suspicious events from the logs.
Task 2 – Build a Hypothesis
Write a threat hunting hypothesis using this format:
“If __ occurs, it may indicate __.”
Task 3 – Attack Timeline
Reconstruct the attack step-by-step.
Format:
 
Initial activity
 
Suspicious behaviour
 
Compromise
 
Post-compromise actions
 
Final objective
Task 4 – Indicators of Compromise (IOCs)
Extract at least 5 IOCs from the logs.
Examples:
IP addresses
Commands
Task 5 – Analyst Actions
As a security analyst, explain what you would do:
Immediate actions
(e.g., isolate system)
Investigation actions
(e.g., check logs, identify scope)
Prevention actions
(e.g., enable MFA)
Task 6 – Threat Hunting Extension
Assume this attacker is still in the network.
What additional logs or data would you check to continue hunting?
